Create or update focused tests first for task {{inputs.taskId}} in {{inputs.worktreePath}}.
Specification:
{{inputs.taskSpec}}
Scope hints:
- Crate: {{inputs.crate}}
- Relevant files: {{inputs.filePaths}}
Add the minimum test coverage needed to define the expected behavior before implementation, keep changes scoped, and summarize what the tests cover.
Do not touch git.

Implement task {{inputs.taskId}} in {{inputs.worktreePath}} so the newly authored tests pass.
Specification:
{{inputs.taskSpec}}
Scope hints:
- Crate: {{inputs.crate}}
- Relevant files: {{inputs.filePaths}}
Use predecessor context from the test-authoring stage, keep the implementation focused, run scoped tests, and summarize the changes plus verification performed.
Do not touch git.

Perform an adversarial audit of task {{inputs.taskId}} using predecessor context and the current worktree.
Worktree: {{inputs.worktreePath}}
Crate: {{inputs.crate}}
Relevant files: {{inputs.filePaths}}
Check for logic flaws, spec gaps, security issues, and whether the implementation genuinely satisfies the tests-first intent.
Return ONLY valid JSON in this shape:
{"verdict":"PASS"|"FAIL","summary":"...","findings":["..."],"commands":["..."]}

